	(text_box "I_LED = VA2 / 10 Ω = 0 to 48 mA, linear in the DAC code (DC coupled, so a code of 8192 is a 24 mA bias and a sine on top of it is intensity modulation). JP9 picks the on-board red LED or your own LED on J10 (anode to +5 V, cathode to the\ndriver). Bandwidth is set by the transistor and the OPA2810, a few MHz."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 299.72 299.72 0)
		(size 180.34 6.35)
		(margins 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525)
		(stroke
			(width 0)
			(type default)
		)
		(fill
			(type color)
			(color 255 255 194 1)
		)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 0.95 0.95)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "08986d19-5c8e-ac5f-4eb5-bdd09d2b40b6")
	)
	(text_box "The FPGA writes 14 bits per port with its own WRT and CLK (dual-port mode; drive MODE low and the same four pins become IQWRT/IQCLK/IQRESET/IQSEL for interleaved I/Q). Each DAC sources 0-19.2 mA into 24.9 Ω (0-0.48 V) on complementary outputs; an OPA2810 takes the difference with gain 4, so the output swings ±2 V open-circuit, ±1 V into 50 Ω, DC coupled and centred on 0 V. 2 kΩ || 2.2 pF rolls\nthe stage off at about 13 MHz with the OPA2810. Channel 2's unipolar node also feeds a voltage-to-current stage that drives an LED (on board, or your own on J10) for the optical experiments."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 20.32 25.4 0)
		(size 340.36 6.35)
		(margins 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525)
		(stroke
			(width 0)
			(type default)
		)
		(fill
			(type color)
			(color 255 255 194 1)
		)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.1 1.1)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "d7640c1c-0bcb-aa9b-4249-3c0e776b42b9")
	)
	(text_box "Timing: data is latched by WRT and the DAC updates on CLK; tie them to the same FPGA clock for the simple case. 14 bits at 125 MSPS straight-binary (code 0 = IOUTA off = -2 V out)."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 20.32 340.36 0)
		(size 160.02 5.08)
		(margins 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525)
		(stroke
			(width 0)
			(type default)
		)
		(fill
			(type color)
			(color 255 255 194 1)
		)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 0.95 0.95)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "f7bb5d0e-0914-745d-f8ea-2a9bc9a4862c")
	)
